// QUARTZFANG DR-01: Interpreter or shell started by cron on the portal
// Author: Károly Mathe | Hunt: Operation QUARTZFANG (HUNT-05), simulated environment
// ATT&CK: T1053.003, T1059.006 | Severity: High | Status: Tested
// Purpose: Cron launching python, perl, sh, bash or nc on the web portal. In the QUARTZFANG hunt this caught the reverse shell (PID 4401) that cron started seconds after the gopher:// request to Redis (the cron write itself is inferred: Redis is not logged).
// Validation: Attack window 2026-09-20 06:30 to 08:30: 1 hit (06:52:52, true positive). Baseline 2026-09-15 to 2026-09-20 06:30: 0 hits in 1,219 process events. After the window: 0 hits in 359 events.
// Blind spots: Estates that run every cron job through /bin/sh -c would flood this rule; add a command-line filter (socket, connect) there. Systemd timers and compiled binaries do not match.
// Schedule: every 1 hour, look back 1 hour
DeviceProcessEvents_CL
| where Timestamp > ago(1h)
| where DeviceName =~ "sc-portal01"
| where InitiatingProcessFileName =~ "cron"
| where FileName in~ ("python3", "python", "perl", "sh", "bash", "nc")
| project Timestamp, DeviceName, AccountName, FileName, ProcessId, ProcessCommandLine
